  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strategic Partnership for Enhancing Security Sector Governance between DSH and the Geneva Centre for Security Sector Governance (DCAF) - Phase III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is phase III of the Strategic Partnership between DSH and DCAF. It covers the period July 2026 - December 2030. 

The partnership is aligned with the DCAF Strategy 2025-2030 and contributes to the objective of &quot;ensuring an effective, accountable, and inclusive security sector that is professional and transparent, and which has full respect for human rights and the rule of law&quot;. This overall objective is promoted through the advancement of three outcome-level objectives:

1: State and non-state actors adopt, adhere to, and implement the principles of good Security Sector Governance and Reform (SSG/R).
2: Multilateral, regional, national and sub-national policies and approaches to SSG/R are strengthened, evidence-based, and effectively applied.
3: Evidence and knowledge generated from programming and research on SSG/R shape global understanding and responses to security challenges.

The Strategic Partnership consists of four components: in-country programming; evidence &amp; knowledge; policy influencing; and policy &amp; practice. In-country programming is foreseen for fifteen countries in the Middle East, North Africa and West Africa. A small part of the funding for components 1 and 2 is allocated to a &quot;Pooled Fund&quot; which combines funding from multiple donors and is administered jointly through the International Parners Group (IPG) Core Group.

In addition to this, the partnership allocates dedicated funding to partnership management and MEAL (monitoring, evaluation, accountability and learning). The MEAL Framework is aligned with DSH&apos;s Security &amp; Rule of Law Results Framework (SROL RF 2023).

The partnership structure is in line with the new modalities for programming set out in the &quot;Besluit aanpak toekomstige programmering en modaliteiten voor Veiligheid en Stabiliteit&quot; of 30 July 2025 and subsequent guidance. All central and in-country programming by DCAF will take place within the framework of this partnership - with the exception of Stability Fund projects outside of the three BHOS focal regions.

A direct grant is being awarded to DCAF with the approval of Director DSH (beslisnota BZ2626495) on the basis of a so-called market scan on SSG/R.</narrative>
  </description>
